    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d152">

                <pb facs="0210" n="200" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg200"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.58112A/11–1844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Sweden</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-12T18:00:00-04:00">December 12,
                            1944—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2496. It now appears likely that the policy with regard to treatment of
                    collaborationists and their properties will be that described <pb facs="0211"
                        n="201" xml:id="pg201"/> in London’s 731, November 18, to you.<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d152-f1"/> Department considers it vitally important that an
                    intelligence operation such as that undertaken with regard to Norway and Denmark
                    be conducted in cooperation with the governments primarily concerned and the
                    British. In view of the British position and that previously displayed by the
                    Norwegians, the Department believes after careful consideration that the
                    Legation’s project for collecting data on Norwegian and Danish collaborators
                    should be abandoned.</p>
                <p>Repeated to London as no. 10369 of December 12.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d152-f1" n="6" xml:id="d152-f1-content">
                <p>See last paragraph of telegram 10139, November 18, 8 p.m., from London, <ref
                        target="#pg197">p. 197</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
